<title>USA: Aracruz doubles share-to-ADR ratio.</title>
<headline>Aracruz doubles share-to-ADR ratio.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian pulp and paper company Aracruz Celulose SA has doubled the ratio of shares to its American Depositary Receipts, J.P. Morgan said on Monday.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that each ADR now represented 10 class B shares of Aracruz. The ratio had been one to five.</p>
<p>The ADRs were trading at 18-1/2. They closed on Friday at 9-3/8.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan is the new depositary bank for Aracruz's ADRs. The previous depositary bank was Bank of New York.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
